Explain purchase-to-payment without inventing authority — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Procurement P1–P5, September 2026
P1: Requester records business need. P2: Procurement issues approved purchase order. P3: Receiving records receipt. P4: AP matches invoice to order and receipt; missing receipt goes to AP exception queue. P5: Treasury releases payment only after separate authorized approval. Glossary: purchase order = purchasing instruction; receipt = evidence of delivery; invoice = supplier payment request; payment approval = separate authority to release funds. Owner: Procurement Operations. No thresholds or holiday calendar supplied.
Task
Northstar is onboarding an FP&A analyst to procurement operations. Learn the process well enough to explain its handoffs.
Actions
	1	Read P1–P5 and identify the input and output of every stage.
	2	Ask AI for a 150-word explanation and one analogy with an explicit limitation.
	3	Trace each process claim to P1–P5; remove any invented threshold.
	4	Hide the response and explain the handoffs from memory in five sentences.
	5	Reopen the reference, correct missing handoffs, and record two questions the reference cannot answer.
Output
Plain-language explanation; analogy and limit; five-stage map; two unanswered policy questions.
